invariant: INV-16
file: srv_resume.c
catches: test/lint-invariants.sh
reason: the binder is compared with memcmp instead of ct_memeq. memcmp returns
  at the first differing byte, so a client that can repeat a ClientHello
  learns how many leading bytes of its binder were right and can search
  for the binder one byte at a time. The comparison is the only
  secret-dependent step in the selection, which is why the rule and not a
  test is what catches it, the way srv-cookie-memcmp is caught.

--- old
        equal = ct_memeq(want, binder, hash_len);
--- new
        equal = (uint32_t)(memcmp(want, binder, hash_len) == 0);
